{"data": {"acceptance": ["For status=repair_required with recovered_operations containing chunking, declining repair displays the localized recovery information exactly once before the repair question.", "After that decline, the project remains unopened and repair_project is not called.", "For the same combined recovery-and-repair result, accepting repair still repairs and activates the project and displays the recovery information exactly once.", "Ordinary successful project opening and recovery without follow-up repair retain their existing behavior without duplicate notices.", "The self-heal remains automatic and post-hoc; no pre-confirmation, combined dialog, logging change, or localization-copy change is introduced.", "The existing UX requirement is updated rather than duplicated, with exact affected paths, focused linked tests, and a companion spec reference; Project Lifecycle documentation describes the ordering guarantee.", "Focused project-flow tests, the repository pytest gate, Ruff gate, traceability audit, and coverage audit pass."], "assumptions": ["The existing localized recovery title and message remain the approved operator copy.", "The recovery information dialog is shown exactly once before the follow-up repair confirmation whenever recovered_operations contains chunking, regardless of the repair choice.", "Declining the follow-up repair continues to leave the project unopened and must not invoke repair_project."], "created_at": "2026-07-30T11:48:33+00:00", "decision": "proceed", "open_questions": [], "planned_paths": ["04_Software/AudioMancer/src/audiomancer/ui/controllers/home_ui_controller.py", "04_Software/AudioMancer/tests/test_main_window_project_flow.py", ".agentic/requirements/ux/REQ-UX-c62252e7-2325-40cf-bf01-4701a429fc9d.toml", ".agentic/specs/cleanup_chunking.spec.md", ".agentic/knowledge/components/Project_Lifecycle.md"], "reason": "The ticket defines the desired ordering and explicitly excludes changing self-heal consent semantics. The implementation is a localized controller sequencing correction with deterministic UI regression coverage and no open product decision.", "recommended_responses": [], "risk": "low", "scope": ["In scope: reorder the existing Home recovery notification relative to the repair confirmation, add focused UI regression coverage, update the existing durable UX requirement and companion Cleanup/Chunking specification, and update Project Lifecycle documentation. Out of scope: service-level reset semantics, pre-confirmation for self-heal, new or combined dialogs, localization copy changes, logger changes, or other issue #40 tickets."], "source": "Gitea issue #34, prioritized by tracking issue #40 and read through authenticated tea CLI", "understanding": "When project opening has already self-healed incompatible Chunking data and the revalidation result also requires a separate manifest repair, Home must disclose the completed destructive reset before asking about that follow-up repair. Declining repair keeps the project unopened but must not suppress the recovery notice; accepting repair continues the established repair and activation flow without a duplicate notice."}, "event": "alignment.recorded", "time": "2026-07-30T11:48:33+00:00"}
